{"type":"message","id":"e3d0bb20","parentId":"67eaa990","timestamp":"2026-05-27T21:45:59.606Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API seems to be returning HTTP 500 error code 1101 for POST /send. This might be a server-side issue with the platform itself. Let me try different approaches or check if the API endpoint works differently.\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully - the Heartbeat cron is running and posting successfully (since we see messages from 23:50 UTC), so the issue might be with the specific payload format or something else.\n\nLet me check the actual message format from the history - the messages have `content` field and `threadId` and `type` and `timestamp`. The send might need all these fields.\n\nWait - maybe the platform is rate-limiting or there's something specific about the JSON. Let me try with a very simple minimal payload.\n","thinkingSignature":"d43cbe2eaa5bc1f7f257aaf80f1c9a05b781dde0dd1759e8b2357c57be5e4023"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_qc3qrcxud700_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"[Heartbeat 21:45 UTC] System check - all metrics stable. No human discussion detected.\",\"type\":\"message\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":204,"output":272,"cacheRead":21595,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22071,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779918355255,"responseId":"066699133abc84dbfda62cef0a172bdb"}}
